0	# InkOS — Sprint 4 Design Spec: Billing & Payments Layer
1	
2	**From:** Vega (Design Agent)
3	**To:** Koda (Feature Builder)
4	**Date:** 2026-04-15
5	**Stack:** Stack A — Next.js 16.2.3, Tailwind 4, shadcn base-nova, dark-first
6	**Sprint:** 4 — Dodo Payments Billing Layer (Week 9–10)
7	
8	---
9	
10	## 0. Pre-Build Rules (carry all 30 from Sprints 1–3 forward, plus these)
11	
12	31. The billing migration `20260415000007_billing_deposits.sql` must be applied and confirmed before Koda writes a single line of billing UI. Tables needed: `subscriptions` (extended), `plans`, `invoices`, `payments`, `usage_meters`, `feature_flags`, `refund_requests`. Dato confirms readiness.
13	32. **Never build a card form.** Every payment action redirects to Dodo hosted checkout or customer portal. `window.location.href = url` is the only checkout pattern.
14	33. All money is stored and transported in cents (`INT`). Display via `formatCurrency(cents)` from `lib/utils.ts`. No template literals, no `$${amount}`. `tabular-nums` on every money value.
15	34. Quota display uses the `usage_meters` table joined to the `plans` table for quota limits. The "used" value is `usage_meters.used`; the quota ceiling is from `plans.sms_monthly_quota` / `plans.ai_generations_quota` / `plans.max_artists` / `plans.max_locations`.
16	35. `UpgradeGate` is a **shared client component** at `components/billing/UpgradeGate.tsx`. It is never a page — it is always rendered inline inside another page's content area, or as a full-page overlay via the modal variant.
17	36. Deposit checkout in the public booking flow is a redirect, not an embedded form. The public booking page POSTs to `/api/public/bookings/[token]/checkout` → receives `{ checkout_url }` → `window.location.href = checkout_url`.
18	37. After deposit redirect returns (Dodo `success_url` → `/book/[studioSlug]/[serviceId]/confirmation?token=[token]`), the confirmation page polls `/api/public/bookings/[token]` every 2s for up to 10s, checking `deposit_paid === true`. If still unpaid after 10s, fall back to a "payment received" message (Dodo webhook may be slightly delayed).
19	38. The refund flow creates a row in `refund_requests` and calls the Dodo refund API server-side. It does NOT manipulate `payments` or `bookings` tables directly from the client.
20	39. `cancel_at_period_end` is set to `true` on cancellation — not instant deletion. The subscription stays `active` until `current_period_end`. Only then does the webhook flip status to `canceled`.
21	40. Admin billing at `/admin/billing` uses the same `shadcn Sidebar` system as the user-facing app layout (per feedback rule from session 7). The admin billing content tabs into the existing admin layout — no new layout wrapper needed.
22	
